  "title": "Okuni and the beginnings of kabuki",
  "summary": "In 1603 the dancer Okuni, tradition says from Izumo, performed in Kyoto at the Kitano Tenmangu shrine and on the banks of the Kamo River in a style she is said to have named kabuki. A screen in the Kyoto National Museum shows her troupe on the Kitano noh stage. Authorities banned actresses from the stage in 1629.",
